From 2738fef454b2122f81da88124a8247ad5e52da86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blaise Rideout <blaise@blaise.in>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:48:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: lenovo-yb9-kbdock: Add Yoga Book 9 13IMU9
 (83FF)

The Yoga Book 9 13IMU9 (DMI product name 83FF) exposes the same WMI
interfaces the driver uses on the 14IAH10: the LENOVO_BTKBD_EVENT event
GUID 806BD2A2-177B-481D-BFB5-3BA0BB4A2285 (notify ID 0xEB) and the
LENOVO_FEATURE_STATUS_DATA block GUID E7F300FA-21CD-4003-ADAC-2696135982E6
(object ID AF), both on the WM10 ACPI device with _UID "GMZN". Without the
DMI match the module is auto-loaded from the event GUID alias but its init
silently returns -ENODEV.

Add 83FF to the DMI table and mention the model in the Kconfig help.

Signed-off-by: Blaise Rideout <blaise@blaise.in>
---
NOT TESTED ON HARDWARE YET: do not send until Tested-by is confirmed.
Still to confirm on a 13IMU9 with the patched module loaded: that the
block driver probes (wmidev_query_block returns id 0x00060000), that
keyboard_position reads 0 with the keyboard detached and 1/2 when docked
in each position, and that event 0xEB fires on dock/undock. Fill this
section in with the observed results before sending.
---
 drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/Kconfig      | 7 ++++---
 drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/yb9-kbdock.c | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/Kconfig b/drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/Kconfig
index 5165949..2d176c2 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/Kconfig
@@ -50,9 +50,10 @@ config LENOVO_YB9_KBDOCK
 	depends on INPUT
 	help
 	  Say Y here to enable keyboard dock detection on the Lenovo Yoga Book 9
-	  14IAH10.  The detachable Bluetooth keyboard magnetically attaches to
-	  either screen; this driver reports SW_TABLET_MODE input events based
-	  on the attachment state and exposes the raw position in sysfs.
+	  14IAH10 and 13IMU9.  The detachable Bluetooth keyboard magnetically
+	  attaches to either screen; this driver reports SW_TABLET_MODE input
+	  events based on the attachment state and exposes the raw position in
+	  sysfs.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
 	  called lenovo-yb9-kbdock.
diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/yb9-kbdock.c b/drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/yb9-kbdock.c
index 70d81f3..7caad14 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/yb9-kbdock.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/lenovo/yb9-kbdock.c
@@ -287,6 +287,13 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id yb9_kbdock_dmi_table[] __initconst = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "83KJ"),
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		/* Lenovo Yoga Book 9 13IMU9 */
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR,   "LENOVO"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "83FF"),
+		},
+	},
 	{ }
 };
 
